build: 2026-06-23 v10.56.0 (Sessions — share / import as portable .echoel.json documents)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: First slice of the founder's "Sessions geräteübergreifend speichern bzw. mit der Community teilen" — dependency-free, no Info.plist/entitlement change. A saved project is already a self-contained Codable value (style · key · tempo · synth patch · notes · drum grid), so the Open-project sheet now: (1) shares any saved session via the standard ShareLink as a portable "<name>.echoel.json" file (AirDrop / Files / Messages / cloud) — encoded lazily on demand via a Transferable wrapper, never on list render; (2) imports a shared session via a .json file picker, giving it a FRESH id so importing never overwrites the original. This is the cross-device + community-sharing foundation using only Apple frameworks. Real-time Live Colabo (Ableton Link tempo sync) still needs founder dependency sign-off; cross-device sync via CloudKit/Multipeer needs config sign-off — both logged. Round-trip + fresh-id + invalid-data tests run on Linux ci.yml; the SwiftUI share/import wiring is validated by the iOS compile gate.
